From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 01:16:17 +0200
Subject: phy: sun4i-usb: Force session end on role changes entering/leaving
 host

usb_add_hcd() sets PHY_MODE_USB_HOST on all phys of a host controller,
so the EHCI0/OHCI0 probes flip phy0's dr_mode to host and re-route it
away from musb when they come up after boot.  When the type-c driver
then sets the role back to device, the id 0 -> 1 transition clears the
musb session while the forced vbus_det stays 1 the whole time - no
vbus edge, so musb never restarts the session and the gadget stays
invisible until the cable is physically replugged.  This is why
rebooting with the cable attached ends with no device on the host.

Mirror sun4i_usb_phy_set_mode() in the role_set callback: force a full
id reprocess and a session end pulse for transitions entering/leaving
host routing.  NONE <-> DEVICE changes keep the fast path since the
vbus_det edge covers them.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c | 19 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun4i-usb.c
@@ -709,6 +709,25 @@ static int sun4i_usb_role_set(struct usb_role_switch *sw, enum usb_role role)
 {
 	struct sun4i_usb_phy_data *data = usb_role_switch_get_drvdata(sw);
 
+	/*
+	 * When the port stops being routed to the host controllers (id 0 -> 1)
+	 * the forced vbus_det typically stays 1 the whole time, so musb never
+	 * sees a vbus edge and its session stays dead -- the gadget does not
+	 * come up until the cable is physically replugged.  This happens e.g.
+	 * on boot with the cable attached: EHCI0/OHCI0 probe flips phy0 to
+	 * host mode via usb_add_hcd()'s phy_set_mode(PHY_MODE_USB_HOST)
+	 * before the type-c driver claims the role switch.  Mirror
+	 * sun4i_usb_phy_set_mode(): force a full id reprocess and a session
+	 * end (vbus_det pulse) for transitions that enter or leave host
+	 * routing.  Plain NONE <-> DEVICE changes keep the fast path, the
+	 * vbus_det edge alone is enough there.
+	 */
+	if (data->usb_role != role &&
+	    (role == USB_ROLE_HOST || data->id_det == 0)) {
+		data->id_det = -1;
+		data->force_session_end = true;
+	}
+
 	data->usb_role = role;
 	queue_delayed_work(system_wq, &data->detect, 0);
 
-- 
